# [claude] What must not reach the build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the one that matters. Size: the context is
# tarred and sent to the daemon on every build, so `.git` and a local
# virtualenv make an otherwise fast rebuild slow. And secrecy: a `COPY . .`
# takes whatever is here, so anything holding a credential or customer data
# has to be excluded at this layer rather than trusted not to be copied.

# Secrets. `.env.*.example` is deliberately kept — it is a template with no
# values, and it documents the variables the image expects.
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example

# Development key material.
var/dev-jwt/
*.pem

# Customer data: uploaded spreadsheets and PDFs, and the vector store built
# from them.
var/

# Local Python state.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# History and tooling that the running app never reads.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.claude/
.langgraph_api/

# Tests, evals and docs. The image runs the application; it does not run
# the suite. CI does that, from the repository, where the whole context is
# present.
tests/
evals/
docs/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
